    slug: 'south-dakota-huron-morales-ortiz-contractor-fraud',
    description: `Julio Morales-Ortiz, 34, ran a roofing and painting business in Huron, South Dakota and, between 2021 and 2023, took payment from at least seven customers for construction work he never completed, according to South Dakota Attorney General Marty Jackley's office. Customers paid Morales-Ortiz up front for roofing and painting jobs on their homes, but the work was left unfinished or never started while he kept the money, leaving victims out more than $36,000 combined with damaged or unrepaired property to show for it. Morales-Ortiz pleaded guilty to one count of theft by deception, and in September 2025 he was sentenced to a 10-year prison term that was suspended down to 15 days in the Beadle County jail, three years of probation, and an order to pay $36,450 in restitution to his victims. Announcing the sentence, Attorney General Jackley said that "when fraudulent contractors and businesses steal from those who hire them, they violate the trust of those who paid them," and his office's Consumer Protection Division urges South Dakotans hiring a contractor to check references and licensing before paying anything, to avoid paying the full cost of a job up front, and to put payment schedules tied to completed work in writing — and to report any contractor who takes payment and disappears to the Attorney General's Consumer Protection Division at 1-800-300-1986.`,
